Verifying known values:
F(1) = 2 (expected 2)
F(3) = 3 (expected 3)
F(9) = 6 (expected 6)
F(11) = 7 (expected 7)
F(100) = 30 (expected 30)
F(50000) = 1898 (expected 1898)

Analysis:
F(N) is the maximum length of a strictly convex chain
of integer points in [0,N]×[0,N].
This is equivalent to the longest chain in the Farey/Stern-Brocot
sequence constrained by the N×N bounding box.

For N=10^18: F(N) = 1398582231101
